{"name":"Beni Shoga","hex":"#b85241","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Beni shōga","blocks":[{"text":"Beni shōga (紅生姜) is a type of tsukemono. It is made from thin strips of ginger pickled in umezu (梅酢), the vinegary pickling solution used to make umeboshi. The red color is traditionally derived from red perilla. Commercial beni shōga often derives its hue from artificial coloring. It is served with many Japanese dishes, including gyūdon, okonomiyaki, and yakisoba."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Gyudon_by_jetalone_in_Higashi-Ginza%2C_Tokyo.jpg/330px-Gyudon_by_jetalone_in_Higashi-Ginza%2C_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beni_sh%C5%8Dga","wikidata":"Q817282"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Woman's shirt from Kutch, Gujarat, India, IMA 55114","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Woman%27s_shirt_from_Kutch%2C_Gujarat%2C_India%2C_IMA_55114.jpg/500px-Woman%27s_shirt_from_Kutch%2C_Gujarat%2C_India%2C_IMA_55114.jpg","ratio":0.9394273127753304,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woman%27s_shirt_from_Kutch,_Gujarat,_India,_IMA_55114.jpg","share":0.134375},{"title":"Two blue water meters on a matte red painted brick facade with pipes in Seoul","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Two_blue_water_meters_on_a_matte_red_painted_brick_facade_with_pipes_in_Seoul.jpg/500px-Two_blue_water_meters_on_a_matte_red_painted_brick_facade_with_pipes_in_Seoul.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Two_blue_water_meters_on_a_matte_red_painted_brick_facade_with_pipes_in_Seoul.jpg","share":0.095},{"title":"Soba kabayaki by nyaa birdies perch in Nakanojo, Gunma","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Soba_kabayaki_by_nyaa_birdies_perch_in_Nakanojo%2C_Gunma.jpg/500px-Soba_kabayaki_by_nyaa_birdies_perch_in_